# Svelte 5

Use Svelte 5 runes and modern patterns. Validate with the Svelte MCP `svelte-autofixer` before finishing.

## Runes

- Props: `$props()` with typed `Props`; use `$bindable()` for two-way bindings
- State: `$state()` for reactive values; `$state.raw()` for large objects/arrays that are reassigned, not mutated
- Derived: `$derived` / `$derived.by` — prefer over `$effect` for computed values
- Effects: `$effect` only as an escape hatch; avoid updating state inside effects
- Events: `onclick`, `onchange`, etc. — not `on:click`
- Composition: `{#snippet}` / `{@render}` for flexible child content

Put reusable reactive logic in `.svelte.ts` classes or modules, not legacy stores.

## Markup and tooltips

- Prefer Svelte snippets and markup over building HTML strings in JavaScript (React-style). Use `{#snippet}`, `{@render}`, and `{#each}` / `{#if}` instead of string concatenation, `escapeHtml`, or `{@html}` for UI you control.
- For `@attach tooltip(...)`, pass plain strings for simple text. For structured tooltip content, use `tooltipSnippet(snippet, arg)` from `@stream-kit/ui/attachments` (one snippet argument; pass an object when you need multiple values) — never assemble tooltip HTML in a callback.

## bits-ui (preferred for UI primitives)

Use `bits-ui` for headless, accessible components instead of building from scratch.

**Already used in this project** — extend these before adding new primitives:

| Need                | bits-ui               |
| ------------------- | --------------------- |
| Dialog / modal      | `Dialog`              |
| Dropdown            | `DropdownMenu`        |
| Select              | `Select`, `Combobox`  |
| Checkbox / switch   | `Checkbox`, `Switch`  |
| Label               | `Label`               |
| Scroll area         | `ScrollArea`          |
| IDs / merging props | `useId`, `mergeProps` |

Wrap `bits-ui` in `@stream-kit/ui/` with project styling (`cn`, Tailwind). Use `WithoutChildren` / `WithoutChild` types when forwarding props. Follow existing patterns in `@stream-kit/ui` input components, dropdown menus, and app modal shell.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import type { WithoutChildren } from 'bits-ui';

	import { Select, useId } from 'bits-ui';

	type Props = {
		id?: string;
		contentProps?: WithoutChildren<Select.ContentProps>;
	} & WithoutChildren<Select.RootProps>;

	let { id = useId(), contentProps, ...props }: Props = $props();
</script>

<Select.Root {...props}>
	<!-- styled sub-components -->
</Select.Root>
```

Check `@stream-kit/ui` and `$lib/components/core/` before creating new interactive UI.

## runed (preferred for reactive utilities)

Use `runed` instead of hand-rolled `$effect` / DOM listeners when a utility exists:

| Need                                | runed                                                            |
| ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| React to value changes              | `watch`                                                          |
| Debounced/throttled values          | `Debounced`, `Throttled`, `useDebounce`, `useThrottle`           |
| Click outside, resize, intersection | `onClickOutside`, `useResizeObserver`, `useIntersectionObserver` |
| Previous value                      | `Previous`                                                       |
| Persisted state                     | `persistedState`                                                 |
| Element/focus tracking              | `activeElement`, `isFocusWithin`, `elementSize`                  |

```ts
import { watch } from 'runed';

watch(
	() => someValue,
	(value) => {
		/* side effect */
	}
);
```

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import { Debounced } from 'runed';

	const debouncedQuery = new Debounced(() => query, 150);
</script>
```

## General

- Match surrounding code: imports, `cn()`, Iconify icons, TypeScript strictness
- Prefer extending existing UI components over duplicating markup
- Use Svelte MCP docs (`list-sections` → `get-documentation`) when unsure about Svelte 5 APIs
- Always use the i18n internationalization system whenever displaying user-facing strings.
- When introducing new strings, ensure they are added to the appropriate translation files, so all languages remain up-to-date.
- Do not hardcode visible text. Instead, wrap strings in the translation function (e.g., `t('Your string here')`) and register those keys for translation management.
- Before creating a new interactive or visual component, always search for and use existing components from the UI library (such as `@stream-kit/ui` or, where appropriate, `$lib/components/core/`). This promotes design consistency and minimizes unnecessary duplication.
- When adding new UI elements, adhere strictly to the established color palette and style tokens for indicating status: use the predefined success, warning, and danger/destructive color classes provided by the UI system.
- If a required component does not exist, consider extending an existing one to preserve consistent UX patterns. Only implement a custom solution when no suitable UI library component is available, and consult with the design system documentation if unsure about color or style usage.
